"""Remove the final review's identified zero-after-abort preference in the document."""
from pathlib import Path
p=Path(__file__).with_name('mechanism.html');s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8')
s=s.replace('suspend object-directed closure and end this goal-evaluation period as an identity-loss event; reacquire the object through the existing protective/exploration path. Record the retained intention for possible later reacquisition under a new period, never silently continue its old value window.', 'suspend object-directed closure, mark this intention period failed, and use the existing protective path for the rest of its period. Retain g and a failure flag in its record so later measured costs are still attributed to this attempt. A new attempt to reacquire the object starts a new period, not a silently repaired old identity.')
s=s.replace('or end it on harm/identity loss; they do not change its value target.', 'or enter its failed protective branch on harm/identity loss; they do not replace g or erase its later measured costs.')
s=s.replace('Missing identity or required fields invalidate this calculation.', 'Missing identity or required fields invalidate ordinary object-directed scoring. On a failed attempt, preserve the last valid unmet-goal distance as evidence and define each subsequent potential increment to be zero, including the transition into failure. Do not set phi to zero and accidentally award the same progress as satisfying the goal. The failure flag selects this branch explicitly; the valid-state telescoping formula applies only while the relationship is observable.')
start=s.index('The value target here counts utility while this goal-evaluation period is active,')
end=s.index('A true completed physical episode likewise has no tail.',start)+len('A true completed physical episode likewise has no tail.')
s=s[:start]+'''The value target counts actual utility throughout the six-second intention period, including failure and protective recovery. At its scheduled end the finite horizon is exhausted. Harm requiring protection or loss of identity stops object-directed commands but does not erase later costs: retain g with a failure flag, run the frozen protective policy, and collect its actual channels to the period end. These failed-branch windows are valid targets for the defined policy. Potential increments are zero during the failure branch rather than a jump to the satisfied-goal potential. Include failed periods in the dataset. If the physical world ends before those readings exist, retain the last harm reading and a censored-window flag; do not fabricate the remaining return or teach a complete h target. Such incomplete attempts still count as physical failures in the ability/adoption comparison. Normal achievement keeps the relationship-maintenance chooser active and supplies actual maintenance windows.''' +s[end:]
s=s.replace('A physical fault records actual harm and ends the physical episode as well as the goal period.', 'A physical fault that ends the world records actual harm and censors the unfinished duration target, as above; it is never removed from the physical failure count.')
s=s.replace('A true completed episode has no tail.', 'A completed requested value horizon has no tail.')
s=s.replace('At an absorbing terminal state phi is zero.', 'At the planned evaluation boundary the remaining horizon is zero. Do not insert an artificial final potential jump; use the last actual relationship for the final valid increment. Failure follows the separate zero-increment rule above.')
s=s.replace('Only at an absorbing end with zero final potential does that term reduce to a fixed starting offset.', 'A failed branch stops adding potential increments; it is not treated as satisfaction. Predicted harm, lost identity or mandatory missing observations disqualify a planned object-directed sequence before scoring, so a favorable utility total cannot authorize a predicted abort.')
s=s.replace('This is how a later result changes an earlier value estimate.', 'This is how a later result changes an earlier value estimate. Adoption also compares physical termination rate, identity-loss rate and observed harm against the same-state reference; reject a producer/chooser that increases any of these beyond the declared matched uncertainty, even if its average value score improves. Censored runs are reported separately and cannot improve success rates by disappearing.')
p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
print('Failure utility retained through observed protective continuation')
